# Scratch-file patterns are ANCHORED with a leading slash. A pattern with no
# slash matches at ANY depth: a bare junit.xml in a product .gitignore silently
# excluded a required committed fixture in P060 of this mission, and a cold
# clone then failed with 17 failures and 9 errors while every local check
# passed. validation/validate_tree_hygiene.py checks both directions with the
# .gitignore semantics re-implemented, because the build agent for this product
# is forbidden from running git.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
/build/
/dist/
/.venv/
/venv/
/.pytest_cache/
/.hypothesis/
/.ruff_cache/
/.coverage
/htmlcov/
/junit.xml
/.config/
# This product serialises NO model: a scikit-learn pickle is not portable
# across minor versions. These patterns exist so a future change cannot add one
# silently, and validation/validate_tree_hygiene.py checks the tree for them.
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.joblib
*.pkl
# The recorded run history IS the evidence this product asserts on. It is
# 402100 bytes, under the mission's 1 MB limit, and it must reach a cold clone:
# every number in README.md, VALIDATION.md and MODEL_CARD.md is a function of
# it, and validation/validate_history.py pins its SHA-256. Listed as negations
# so that a future broad pattern cannot swallow them silently.
!/data/run_history.json
!/data/generate_history.py
!/data/generate_history_output.txt
# Every validation script's raw output is evidence and must ship.
!/validation/*_output.txt
